      en: "Folkestone Marine Park, located on the west coast of Barbados in St. James, was established in 1981. It covers 6.5 hectares of coastal area, including a coral reef, seagrass beds, and a sheltered bay. The park is popular for snorkeling and diving, featuring an artificial reef complex made from sunken ships and concrete structures. Marine life includes diverse fish, turtles, and corals. On land, there are picnic areas, a small museum, and a visitor center. The park is managed by the Barbados Marine Trust.",
